    <section class="bio">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p>I'm a Staff Technical Project Manager at SentinelOne, based in Springfield, Missouri. Before that I spent nine years at Block, Jack Henry and Pondurance. My job has always been getting complicated technical work across the finish line: migrations, rollouts and projects that touch a dozen teams.</p>
      <p>In early 2026 that changed. With AI coding tools, mainly Claude Code, I started building the tools myself instead of only coordinating the people who build them. I'm not a traditional software engineer, and I don't pretend to be. What I'm good at is knowing what to build, directing the AI to build it, checking the work, and deciding when it's done or when to walk away.</p>
      <p>That shows up in the work here:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>At Block I built a knowledge base for support agents that went to production, plus the tools that kept a large content migration on track.</li>
        <li>On my own time I built an NBA prediction model that ran live for a season, and a real-time auction draft room for my fantasy football league.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>I'm looking for product, technical program or builder roles where I can do both: figure out the right thing to build, and build it. I'm especially interested in internal tools, customer-facing products, sports tech and weather.</p>
      <p>Outside of work, I'm an avid Chiefs fan. I play golf, travel with my wife, and take care of our two dogs, Zoey and Traeger.</p>
    </section>

